<title>USA: Gap board approves share buyback.</title>
<headline>Gap board approves share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gap Inc said on Wednesday that its board had approved the repurchase of up to 30 million shares of its common stock in the open market over the next three years.</p>
<p>The retailer said the program replaces an 18 million share buyback that was completed this month. The new program is intended, in part, to offset future dilution from stock-based incentive plans, it said.</p>
<p>As of October 5, the end of the most recent fiscal month, Gap had 280.8 million shares outstanding.</p>
</text>
